From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:30:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] kcm: Turn snapping off while Shift is held during a drag

Dragging a screen in the arrangement view snaps it to the edges and
centres of the others within 80 pixels, so a small offset, such as a
screen 60 pixels lower than its neighbour, cannot be made with the mouse.
The arrow keys already move a selected screen pixel by pixel without
snapping; holding Shift now does the same for a drag: the screen goes
where it is dropped, through the model's setPosition() with snapping off.
A line under the arrangement view's heading says so while it is edited.

wdisplays, the wlroots display tool, uses the same modifier; KScreen used
Ctrl for it before its KF5 port (bug 348241, comment 1).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 kcm/ui/Output.qml     |  4 +++-
 kcm/ui/ScreenView.qml | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kcm/ui/Output.qml b/kcm/ui/Output.qml
index 3dca479c..6a7b0f6e 100644
--- a/kcm/ui/Output.qml
+++ b/kcm/ui/Output.qml
@@ -293,7 +293,9 @@ Item {
         onTranslationChanged: {
             var newX = dragStartPosition.x + translation.x;
             var newY = dragStartPosition.y + translation.y;
-            model.position = getAbsolutePosition(Qt.point(newX, newY));
+            // Holding Shift places the screen exactly where it is dropped
+            const snap = !(centroid.modifiers & Qt.ShiftModifier);
+            kcm.outputModel.sourceModel.setPosition(model.index, getAbsolutePosition(Qt.point(newX, newY)), snap);
         }
         onActiveChanged: {
             model.interactiveMove = active;
diff --git a/kcm/ui/ScreenView.qml b/kcm/ui/ScreenView.qml
index 95293e73..6f282e36 100644
--- a/kcm/ui/ScreenView.qml
+++ b/kcm/ui/ScreenView.qml
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ QQC2.ScrollView {
     readonly property int yOffset: (height - totalSize.height / relativeFactor) / 2;
 
     Kirigami.Heading {
+        id: dragHint
         z: 90
         anchors {
             top: parent.top
@@ -62,6 +63,24 @@ QQC2.ScrollView {
         }
     }
 
+    QQC2.Label {
+        z: 90
+        anchors {
+            top: dragHint.bottom
+            left: parent.left
+            right: parent.right
+            leftMargin: Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
+            rightMargin: Kirigami.Units.smallSpacing
+        }
+        horizontalAlignment: Text.AlignHCenter
+        wrapMode: Text.Wrap
+        font: Kirigami.Theme.smallFont
+        text: i18nc("@info:usagetip", "Hold Shift while dragging to place a screen without snapping")
+
+        opacity: dragHint.opacity
+        visible: dragHint.visible
+    }
+
     Repeater {
         model: kcm.outputModel
         delegate: Output {
-- 
